# 46. AI Safety and Reliability

COVE2E must not:

* Guarantee claim approval
* Guarantee payout
* Fabricate policy coverage
* Invent claim requirements
* Make insurer decisions
* Represent assumptions as policy facts
* Silently modify user documents
* Submit claims without appropriate authorization
* Execute unauthorized financial actions
* Treat an LLM response as authoritative evidence

The AI should distinguish between:

### Policy Fact

> "Your policy states..."

### AI Interpretation

> "Based on the available policy information..."

### Missing Information

> "I cannot determine this because..."

### External Decision

> "The insurer will make the final claim decision."

### Recovery Decision

> "COVE2E identified this as the current journey blocker based on the available claim state and requirements."

